      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\text{tr}(A)=5$ and $\\text{det}(A)=9.$ Then, ${A}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =5A-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
